# 109 - aegis-home-dock-fix (fix-forward from r57 user report)
# The user-tested r57 build had three hard defects, all confirmed against
# upstream 156 sources:
#   1. Home never showed: AegisHomeView was added at index 0 of the content
#      root (BEHIND the coordinator's NTP) and its "chrome://newtab" prefix
#      check never matched the native chrome-native://newtab/ URL. Now the
#      home is the LAST child (dock installs right after, still above it),
#      full-screen, consumes stray taps, and detects NTPs with
#      UrlUtilities.isNtpUrl; TabObserver flips it instantly.
#   2. Dock recall dead: the dock root was WRAP_CONTENT (52dp band) while the
#      24x140dp sliver target hung 44dp OUTSIDE the root via a negative
#      margin - those taps fell through to web content. The root is now a
#      full-screen pass-through FrameLayout and the sliver is vertically
#      centered INSIDE it (no negative margin).
#   3. Trust line blank when idle: refreshUrl only bound the page title while
#      loading; it now binds title/host always (hint only with no tab), and
#      navigation events peek the dock via TabObserver (1 Hz poll stays as
#      fallback).

